			},
			"notes": {
				"rationale": "es jemandem recht machen (Wiktionary headword; DWDS: jmdm. etw. recht machen, 'zu jmds. Zufriedenheit erledigen') means to satisfy someone, not the sum of make and right, so it is a Locution VERB (de/idiom). Its es refers to nothing and cannot be swapped for das without losing the meaning, so it is a fixed member (de/fixed-member-test); the dative Ihnen is an open slot, left out of the Canonical Form as ADR 0039 does with auf den Keks gehen. Ruled on #743 (JT-B1, A5)."
			}
		},
